              ],
              "title": "Since the major indices peaked at all-time closing highs (ATHs) on June 2, we have witnessed an increase in price volatility to the downside and the upside. On June 10, the six-day rate-of-change (ROC) on the S&P 500 (SPX) fell to -4.5%. By June 18, it had reversed to +3.2%, and then by June 24 it fell to -2.6%. For the Nasdaq 100 (QQQ), the sequence of six-day returns went from -7% to +6.8% to -4.4%."
